.TH OTS_MM_UDP_INTERFACE 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-CFOControl t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
ots_mm_udp_interface \- Python client for the otsdaq MacroMaker UDP protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B from ots_mm_udp_interface import OtsMMUdpInterface
.B from ots_mm_udp_interface import encode_uri_component, decode_uri_component
.PP
.BI "with OtsMMUdpInterface(" host ", " port ", timeout_first=10.0, timeout_next=0.2, verbose=False) as " mm :
.BI "    mm.get_frontend_list()"
.BI "    mm.get_command_list(" fe )
.BI "    s = mm.build_input_string(" fe ", " command ", " values )
.BI "    outputs = mm.run_command(" fe ", " command ", " s )
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A single-module, standard-library-only port of otsdaq-utilities'
.IR test/ots_mm_udp_interface.cpp .
It speaks the text protocol served by
.B MacroMakerSupervisor::RemoteControlWorkLoop
when the supervisor is started with both
.B OTS_MACROMAKER_UDP_IP
and
.B OTS_MACROMAKER_UDP_PORT
set.
The module is not installed as a package; callers import it from the
directory that contains it.
.PP
Two requests exist.
.B GetFrontendMacroInfo
returns an XML document with one
.B <FEMacros value='...'/>
element per front-end interface, whose value is
.BR ; -separated:
supervisor name, supervisor LID, interface type, interface UID, then
repeated records
.IR "name;permissions;tooltip;nIn;in...;nOut;out..." .
.B RunFrontendMacro;\fItype\fB;\fIuid\fB;fe;\fIenc(name)\fB;\fIinputs\fB;\fIoutputs\fB;0
runs one macro and returns XML containing
.B <outputArgs_value value='...'/>
elements, an XML
.B <Error value='...'/>
element if the macro threw, or the plain text
.B "Error: ..."
for supervisor-level failures.
The full wire description is in
.IR docs/INTERFACES.md .
.SS Class OtsMMUdpInterface
.TP
.BI OtsMMUdpInterface( host ", " port ", " timeout_first ", " timeout_next ", " verbose )
Resolve
.I host
with
.BR getaddrinfo (3)
(first result, IPv4 or IPv6) and open one non-blocking UDP socket.
Usable as a context manager;
.B close()
closes the socket.
.TP
.BI get_frontend_macro_info( force_refresh=False )
Send
.B GetFrontendMacroInfo
and return the concatenated reply.
The reply is cached on the object; later calls return the cache unless
.I force_refresh
is true.
Raises
.B RuntimeError
on an empty reply.
.TP
.B get_frontend_list()
List of front-end UIDs (field 3 of every
.B FEMacros
element).
.TP
.BI get_command_list( fe )
URI-decoded macro names for
.IR fe .
.TP
.BI get_command_input_count( fe ", " command )
.TQ
.BI get_command_output_count( fe ", " command )
.TQ
.BI get_command_input_name( fe ", " command ", " index )
.TQ
.BI get_command_output_name( fe ", " command ", " index )
Parameter metadata parsed from the cached
.B FEMacros
string.
.TP
.BI build_input_string( fe ", " command ", " values )
Return
.IB enc(name1) , enc(value1) ; enc(name2) , enc(value2)...
for plain string
.IR values .
Raises
.B RuntimeError
if the count does not match.
.TP
.BI run_command( fe ", " command ", " inputs )
Send
.B RunFrontendMacro
with
.I inputs
placed verbatim in field 5, and return the list of still URI-encoded
.B outputArgs_value
strings in reply order.
Raises
.B RuntimeError
on an empty reply or an XML
.B <Error>
element.
.TP
.BI decode_outputs( values )
URI-decode a list returned by
.BR run_command .
.SS Module functions
.TP
.BI encode_uri_component( s )
Keep characters for which
.B str.isalpha()
or
.B str.isdigit()
is true; percent-encode every UTF-8 byte of every other character.
Stricter than JavaScript's
.BR encodeURIComponent ,
which also keeps
.BR \-_.!~*'() .
.TP
.BI decode_uri_component( s )
Replace each
.BI % XX
with
.BR chr(0x XX ),
one byte at a time, so multi-byte UTF-8 decodes as Latin-1.
Malformed escapes pass through.
.TP
.BI decode_html_entities( s )
Replace seven common HTML entities.
Not called by the module itself.
.TP
.BI extract_xml_field( xml ", " field ", " occurrence=0 ", " after=0 )
Return
.RI ( value ", " end )
for the
.IR occurrence th
.BI < field " value='" ... "'/>"
at or after offset
.IR after ,
or
.B ("", \-1)
if absent.
This is string search, not an XML parser.
.SH ERRORS
Protocol failures raise
.BR RuntimeError .
Name resolution and socket failures raise
.B OSError
(including
.BR socket.gaierror ).
.SH BUGS
.TP
.B Multi-input framing
.B run_command
does not URI-encode
.I inputs
before inserting it into the
.BR ; -separated
datagram, and
.B build_input_string
joins pairs with a raw
.BR ; .
The MacroMaker splits the whole datagram on
.BR ; ,
so for two or more inputs input 2 becomes the output-name list.
The C++ reference encodes the whole input string a second time.
.TP
.B Plain-text errors
A reply of the form
.B "Error: ..."
returns an empty list instead of raising.
.TP
.B Truncation
A reply ends when no datagram arrives within
.I timeout_next
seconds.
There is no length, sequence number or end-of-document check, so a late or
lost fragment yields a short reply with no exception.
Datagrams are not filtered by source address; on a reused object a late
fragment of one reply is read as the start of the next.
Each
.B recvfrom
reads at most 5000 bytes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
from ots_mm_udp_interface import OtsMMUdpInterface, decode_uri_component
with OtsMMUdpInterface("mu2e\-cfo\-01", 5000) as mm:
    s = mm.build_input_string("CFO0", "CFO Read", ["0x9100"])
    for v in mm.run_command("CFO0", "CFO Read", s):
        print(decode_uri_component(v))
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR CFOControl.py (1),
.BR config.yaml (5)
